    52	
    53	FLAC exp_02 (released FLAC_EMA, unseen K = 1, single runs, no intervals): accuracy degradation vs shift — EDT +3.5 / +6.3 / +4.0 ms vs 18.7 / 20.1 / 20.0 ms (shift-to-degradation 5.4× / 3.2× / 5.0×), T60 +0.39 / +0.73 / +0.45 pp vs 3.3–3.4 %, C50 +0.03 / +0.14 / +0.08 dB vs 0.55–0.60 dB at 90 / 180 / 270°. xRIR released K = 8 (this experiment, intervals above): EDT −1.6 / −1.2 / −0.9 ms vs 24.9 / 25.6 / 23.8 ms, T60 +0.26 / −0.24 / +0.16 pp vs 3.2 / 3.3 / 3.1 %, C50 −0.003 / +0.008 / +0.022 dB vs 0.61 / 0.64 / 0.59 dB. The shift magnitudes are similar across the two families (EDT ≈ 20–26 ms, C50 ≈ 0.6 dB, T60 ≈ 3.3 %), while xRIR's signed net accuracy change is smaller than FLAC's degradation and mixed in sign. Wording that the evidence supports, with its scope stated: *in both families a conditioning yaw rotation, which changes nothing physically, shifts the prediction substantially — EDT by about 20–26 ms, C50 by about 0.6 dB, T60 by about 3.3 % of the baseline prediction's T60 — while the net error against ground truth changes far less. FLAC's single-run degradations are 3–5× smaller than its shifts. For xRIR's released checkpoint at K = 8, of the twelve primary cells (EDT, C50, T60 × four angles) five have a net change not resolvable from zero, three show a net improvement, and four show a net deterioration with a reportable shift-to-change multiple: T60 45° 8.0× [6.1, 11.6] (room-level status defined), T60 90° 12.3× [8.3, 24.3], T60 270° 19.2× [10.6, 71.6] and C50 45° 19.5× [10.3, 85.0] (room-level denominators uncertain).* No universal "order of magnitude" statement is licensed: multiples exist only for named reportable cells, and the room-level caveat travels with them.
    54	
    55	Qualifications that must accompany any cross-family sentence: (i) xRIR's waveform / acoustic gaps include the Griffin-Lim inversion (§2); (ii) both evaluators use the first 8 000 samples at 22 050 Hz (FLAC `src/metrics/metric_callback.py:114`), but FLAC's AcousticRooms path keeps every T60 measurement in its mean, including failed ones carrying the helper's sentinel (`src/metrics/modules/RT60.py`, `update`: no invalid mask for AcousticRooms), whereas xRIR returns NaN and excludes the query; FLAC's C50 adds 1e-10 inside the log10 (`src/metrics/modules/C50.py`), xRIR's `Evaluator` does not — the acoustic gaps are conceptually, not numerically, comparable; (iii) no waveform-distance ranking across families (10 240 decoded samples vs 9 600 inverted samples with 21 padding samples); (iv) FLAC's arm is K = 1 with its own protocol, xRIR's primary is K = 8; xRIR's K = 1 arm is a K = 8-trained model evaluated with one reference; (v) FLAC's numbers are single evaluations without intervals.
